cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "4D-VODS: optical data storage in glass with a self-aligning code for low-cost readers"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24268721
authors:
  - family-names: Guettal
    given-names: Hakim
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GuettHM/4d-vods"
url: "https://guetthm.github.io/4d-vods/"
abstract: >-
  Open simulator and documents for a concept of archival optical data storage
  in glass. It compares an 8-bit asymmetric "Voxel-Wedge" symbol with small
  amplitude/phase (APSK-16) dots under diffraction-limited optics,
  and introduces a Self-Aligning Micro-Matrix (SAMM) code that a low-cost
  bright-field microscope camera can find, orient and decode at any rotation.
  The author is not a professional physicist; the study was built with the help
  of AI tools on standard diffraction optics.
keywords:
  - optical data storage
  - archival storage
  - glass
  - femtosecond laser writing
  - 2D code
  - self-alignment
  - simulation
